      "message": "The device tree for this failing test is defined in `zephyr/test/drivers/usbc_tcpc/tcpc_alts.dts`. Uniquely, this device tree has two compatible strings for most TCPC nodes, the real one from the driver and \"cros,i2c-mock.\" This is to accommodate TCPCs without real Zephyr drivers. The test doesn\u0027t actually need the TCPC emulators, and they aren\u0027t being instantiated in general, because they use different compat strings than the TCPC device nodes.\n\nFor the RAA489000 emulator, you\u0027re using the \"renesas,raa489000\" compat string, which is the right thing to do. However, it causes this device node in this test to have devices and emulators instantiated for it twice, once for each compat string. With your new emulator, the \"cros,i2c-mock\" compat string is redundant.\n\nThe fix is to remove the \"cros,i2c-mock\" compat string for [this node](zephyr/test/drivers/usbc_tcpc/tcpc_alts.dts).\n\nWe could probably clean up further by removing some more \"cros,i2c-mock\" compat strings, but that\u0027s out of scope for this CL. Sorry that this was a stumbling block.",
